{
  "original_id": "win-00068-p07",
  "archive_id": "BW2-B68-P07",
  "title": "A Degree-Four Obstruction to Nonnegative Closure for Independent-Row K-Species",
  "batch_label": "68",
  "kind": "resolution-paper",
  "original_status": "proved",
  "scope": "Under the literal independent-row convention G_alpha=<c_1>x...x<c_k> on disjoint row blocks, every product K_alpha x K_beta for partitions alpha,beta of n has a nonnegative integral K-species coproduct decomposition for n=1,2,3, but K_(2,2) x K_(4) has no such decomposition in degree four. Its unique degree-four cycle-index expansion is 2 K_(2,2) - 2 K_(2,1,1) + 2 K_(1,1,1,1). Therefore degree four is the first failure of nonnegative independent-row K-basis closure, in exactly the sense specified in problem.md; no claim is made about closed formulas in a larger molecular-species basis or the rest of Open Problem 5.1.",
  "gate_basis": "Current released terminal, manifest, PDF, TeX freeze, snapshot files, provenance and four audits agree.",
